                "stdout_tail": "{\"actual_models\": [\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\", \"claude-sonnet-5\"], \"selected_family_models\": [\"claude-sonnet-5\"], \"other_reported_models\": [\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\"], \"verdict\": {\"findings\": [\"Requested check 'Linux and native success conjunction' is not evidenced in either file. bootstrap_controller.rs::Controller::finish() returns success/exit status derived solely from the native child process (WaitForSingleObject + child.wait()), with no reference to the Linux subject's outcome. cross_os_reset.rs::Subject::finish() unconditionally copies the enumerated mailbox files (including seal.json) to the evidence directory without inspecting seal.json's contents or otherwise asserting Linux-side success. Neither file cross-references the other's success/failure state, so the conjunction of Linux and native success cannot be confirmed from this evidence; if it exists it must live in code not provided here.\"], \"summary\": \"Primary-role/finite-timeout validation before spawn, ordinary Job containment (no breakaway/detached launch), and narrow enumerated mailbox export all check out against the provided evidence. The one requested property that could not be confirmed is the conjunction of Linux-subject and native-controller success \\u2014 neither file ties the two outcomes together.\\\"\", \"verdict\": \"findings\"}}\n",
